{:edb/committed true :edb/basis-t 1013 :edb/replayed false :edb/tx-hash "caff3b05caa2968c08dce452abc9eecda148d1ec6add2d042b048636eaa9f9d5" :edb/db-before-t 1012 :edb/db-after-t 1013 :edb/tx-data [[13194139534325 50 #inst "2026-10-06T16:03:21.585Z" 13194139534325 true] [17592186087501 1100 "Consider the linear transformation $\\mathbf T$ with matrix representation $T$, given by\n$\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & -2\\end{bmatrix}$\n\nThe triangle $\\triangle ABC$ is shown below. Find $\\triangle A'B'C'$, the image of $\\triangle ABC$ under the action of $\\mathbf T$.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/866/Source/Images/8d714d1a8dad0fec63191b436f75f1f2.png)" 13194139534325 false] [17592186087501 1100 "Consider the linear transformation $\\mathbf T$ with matrix representation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & -2\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nThe triangle $\\triangle ABC$ is shown below. Find $\\triangle A'B'C',$ the image of $\\triangle ABC$ under the action of $\\mathbf T.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13990291/assets/4986bd2dab6b455c0d5e41909377c433d761bf7270364d3e2596e6db7f23981b.png)" 13194139534325 true] [17592186087501 1145 "To find the image of $T$ under the action of $\\mathbf T$, we first create a matrix $X$ containing all of the vertices of $\\triangle ABC$:\n$\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}$\n\nNow, we compute the image of $X$ under the action of $\\mathbf T$ by calculating the matrix product $TX$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nTX &= \\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & -2\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\\n&= \\begin{bmatrix}-3 & 0 & 1 \\\\ -4 & 0 & -2\\end{bmatrix}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coordinates of the respective vertices of $\\triangle A'B'C'$ are $(-3,-4), (0,0), (1,-2)$, as shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/866/Source/Images/3ac3afc1cb31f4c0e1cf319acf62a417.png)" 13194139534325 false] [17592186087501 1145 "To find the image of $T$ under the action of $\\mathbf T,$ we first create a matrix $X$ containing all of the vertices of $\\triangle ABC\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the image of $X$ under the action of $\\mathbf T$ by calculating the matrix product $TX\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}TX & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & -2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 0 & 1 \\\\ -4 & 0 & -2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coordinates of the respective vertices of $\\triangle A'B'C'$ are $(-3,-4), (0,0), (1,-2),$ as shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13990291/assets/e8a14ffbaab4597a2a4a7c9a6bad61dabbc4970fc22c3ed2eb28b2594a670938.png)" 13194139534325 true] [17592186087547 1100 "Consider the linear transformation $\\mathbf T$ with matrix representation $T$, given by\n\n$\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 3 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{bmatrix}$\n\nThe line segment $\\overline{AB}$ is shown below. Find $\\overline{A'B'}$, the image of $\\overline{AB}$ under the action of $\\mathbf T$.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/866/Source/Images/99de657ac0df287926da7644ba8c7907.png)" 13194139534325 false] [17592186087547 1100 "Consider the linear transformation $\\mathbf T$ with matrix representation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nThe line segment $\\overline{AB}$ is shown below. Find $\\overline{A'B'},$ the image of $\\overline{AB}$ under the action of $\\mathbf T.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13990291/assets/2e22400d15abc81150d6d18de591549e81a46bd16ab9e95f10f86bae2125b490.png)" 13194139534325 true] [17592186087547 1145 "To find the image of $\\overline{AB}$ under the action of $\\mathbf T$, we first create a matrix $X$ containing the coordinates of the endpoints of $\\overline{AB}$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the image of $X$ under the action of $\\mathbf T$ by calculating the matrix product $TX$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nTX &= \\begin{bmatrix}2 & 3 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\\n&= \\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 \\\\ 3 & -2\\end{bmatrix}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coordinates of the respective endpoints of the image are $A'(1,3)$ and $B'(1,-2)$, as shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/866/Source/Images/105a1915ca20d2babc4684b44cd6620a.png)" 13194139534325 false] [17592186087547 1145 "To find the image of $\\overline{AB}$ under the action of $\\mathbf T$, we first create a matrix $X$ containing the coordinates of the endpoints of $\\overline{AB}\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the image of $X$ under the action of $\\mathbf T$ by calculating the matrix product $TX\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}TX & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 3 & -2\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coordinates of the respective endpoints of the image are $A'(1,3)$ and $B'(1,-2),$ as shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13990291/assets/472f8e712f7d695d5ab3593dafbcc0309feb1a6ac80e9e29c4893dc651d20cf7.png)" 13194139534325 true] [17592186087687 1020 #edb/ref 17592186283466 13194139534325 true] [17592186087687 1020 #edb/ref 17592186283492 13194139534325 true] [17592186087687 1020 #edb/ref 17592186283505 13194139534325 true] [17592186087687 1020 #edb/ref 17592186283539 13194139534325 true] [17592186087722 1020 #edb/ref 17592186283473 13194139534325 true] [17592186087722 1020 #edb/ref 17592186283483 13194139534325 true] [17592186087722 1020 #edb/ref 17592186283518 13194139534325 true] [17592186087722 1020 #edb/ref 17592186283525 13194139534325 true] [17592186087722 1020 #edb/ref 17592186283532 13194139534325 true] [17592186087935 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534325 true] [17592186087935 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13990291/assets/205badcabf4c2444f7ca8b38e189b1a0f8957e324ba7fb1a28909dc4afdd8c75.png)\n\nConsider the linear transformation $T$ with matrix representation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nThe triangle $△ABC$ is shown above. Which of the following is $△{A}^{′}{B}^{′}{C}^{′},$ the image of $△ABC$ under the action of $T?$" 13194139534325 true] [17592186087935 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/866/Source/Images/q-12031.png)\n\nConsider the linear transformation $T$ with matrix representation $T$, given by\n$T = \\begin{bmatrix}0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}$.\n\nThe triangle $△ABC$ is shown above. Which of the following is $△A^{′}B^{′}C^{′}$, the image of $△ABC$ under the action of $T$?" 13194139534325 false] [17592186087935 1145 "To find the image of $T$ under the action of $T$, we first create a matrix $X$ containing all of the vertices of $△ABC:$\n\n$$\nX=[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 1 & 3 \\\\ -2 & 2 & -2\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the image of $X$ under the action of $T$ by calculating the matrix product $TX:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}TX & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-3 & 1 & 3 \\\\ -2 & 2 & -2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & -2 & 2 \\\\ -3 & 1 & 3\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, the coordinates of the respective vertices of $△{A}^{′}{B}^{′}{C}^{′}$ are $(2,-3),(-2,1),(2,3)$, as shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13990291/assets/4e456209fc818f606bfe83324b05843b0122840161a84a8d729927f4050f2397.png)" 13194139534325 true] [17592186283466 1017 #edb/ref 17592186283467 13194139534325 true] [17592186283466 1089 "q-159801" 13194139534325 true] [17592186283466 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534325 true] [17592186283466 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13990291/assets/d9ec98b03009d1023668aa12de88ed5515f0ea6df058d1b5d17804bf42082c5c.png)\n\nConsider the linear transformation $T$ with matrix representation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nThe triangle $△ABC$ is shown above. Which of the following is $△{A}^{′}{B}^{′}{C}^{′},$ the image of $△ABC$ under the action of $T?$" 13194139534325 true] [17592186283466 1113 #uuid "b95133b0-1616-5846-9583-0eb3e1ac9ba0" 13194139534325 true] [17592186283466 1145 "To find the image of $T$ under the action of $T$, we first create a matrix $X$ containing all of the vertices of $△ABC:$\n\n$$\nX=[\\begin{aligned}2 & -3 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 2 & -2\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the image of $X$ under the action of $T$ by calculating the matrix product $TX:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}TX & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 0\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}2 & -3 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 2 & -2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}6 & 1 & -3 \\\\ 4 & -6 & 2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coordinates of the respective vertices of $△{A}^{′}{B}^{′}{C}^{′}$ are $(6,4),(1,-6),(-3,2)$, as shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13990291/assets/4c43c4c793924d4fde32b59c93b7a19be0109a389b126665868396b4c06d721e.png)" 13194139534325 true] [17592186283467 1000 #edb/ref 17592186283468 13194139534325 true] [17592186283467 1000 #edb/ref 17592186283469 13194139534325 true] [17592186283467 1000 #edb/ref 17592186283470 13194139534325 true] [17592186283467 1000 #edb/ref 17592186283471 13194139534325 true] [17592186283467 1000 #edb/ref 17592186283472 13194139534325 true] [17592186283467 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534325 true] [17592186283467 1041 "selection" 13194139534325 true] [